{"surah": 72, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "قُلْ أُوحِىَ إِلَىَّ أَنَّهُ ٱسْتَمَعَ نَفَرٌ مِّنَ ٱلْجِنِّ فَقَالُوٓا۟ إِنَّا سَمِعْنَا قُرْءَانًا عَجَبًا ", "translation": "Say, [O Muḥammad], \"It has been revealed to me that a group of the jinn listened and said, 'Indeed, we have heard an amazing Qur’ān [i.e., recitation].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أُوحِىَ", "translit": "َàِḥwُaʾ", "root": "وحي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَىَّ", "translit": "َّàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَنَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱسْتَمَعَ", "translit": "َʿعَmَtْsٱ", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "نَفَرٌ", "translit": "ٌrَfَn", "root": "نفر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْجِنِّ", "translit": "ِّnِjgْlٱ", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فَقَالُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlāَqَf", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "سَمِعْنَا", "translit": "āَnْʿعِmَs", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "قُرْءَانًا", "translit": "āًnāَءْrُq", "root": "قرا"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "عَجَبًا", "translit": "āًbَjgَʿع", "root": "عجب"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "يَهْدِىٓ إِلَى ٱلرُّشْدِ فَـَٔامَنَّا بِهِۦۖ وَلَن نُّشْرِكَ بِرَبِّنَآ أَحَدًا ", "translation": "It guides to the right course, and we have believed in it. And we will never associate with our Lord anyone.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَهْدِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِdْhَy", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلرُّشْدِ", "translit": "ِdْhsُّrlٱ", "root": "رشد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَـَٔامَنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَmāَٔـَf", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَلَن", "translit": "nَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "نُّشْرِكَ", "translit": "َkِrْhsُّn", "root": "شرك"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بِرَبِّنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnِّbَrِb", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَحَدًا", "translit": "āًdَḥَaʾ", "root": "احد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "وَأَنَّهُۥ تَعَٰلَىٰ جَدُّ رَبِّنَا مَا ٱتَّخَذَ صَٰحِبَةً وَلَا وَلَدًا ", "translation": "And [it teaches] that exalted is the nobleness of our Lord; He has not taken a wife or a son", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَعَٰلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَٰʿعَt", "root": "علو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "جَدُّ", "translit": "ُّdَjg", "root": "جدد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "رَبِّنَا", "translit": "āَnِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱتَّخَذَ", "translit": "َhdَhkَّtٱ", "root": "اخذ"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "صَٰحِبَةً", "translit": "ًẗَbِḥَٰṣ", "root": "صحب"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَلَدًا", "translit": "āًdَlَw", "root": "ولد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "وَأَنَّهُۥ كَانَ يَقُولُ سَفِيهُنَا عَلَى ٱللَّهِ شَطَطًا ", "translation": "And that our foolish one [i.e., Iblees][1] has been saying about Allāh an excessive transgression.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَقُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُqَy", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "سَفِيهُنَا", "translit": "āَnُhyِfَs", "root": "سفه"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَلَى", "translit": "àَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "شَطَطًا", "translit": "āًṭَṭَhs", "root": "شطط"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "وَأَنَّا ظَنَنَّآ أَن لَّن تَقُولَ ٱلْإِنسُ وَٱلْجِنُّ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ كَذِبًا ", "translation": "And we had thought that mankind and the jinn would never speak about Allāh a lie.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ظَنَنَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّnَnَẓ", "root": "ظنن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَّن", "translit": "nَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَقُولَ", "translit": "َlwُqَt", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْإِنسُ", "translit": "ُsnِiʾْlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَٱلْجِنُّ", "translit": "ُّnِjgْlٱَw", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَلَى", "translit": "àَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "كَذِبًا", "translit": "āًbِhdَk", "root": "كذب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "وَأَنَّهُۥ كَانَ رِجَالٌ مِّنَ ٱلْإِنسِ يَعُوذُونَ بِرِجَالٍ مِّنَ ٱلْجِنِّ فَزَادُوهُمْ رَهَقًا ", "translation": "And there were men from mankind who sought refuge in men from the jinn, so they [only] increased them in burden [i.e., sin].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رِجَالٌ", "translit": "ٌlāَjgِr", "root": "رجل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْإِنسِ", "translit": "ِsnِiʾْlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَعُوذُونَ", "translit": "َnwُhdwُʿعَy", "root": "عوذ"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِرِجَالٍ", "translit": "ٍlāَjgِrِb", "root": "رجل"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْجِنِّ", "translit": "ِّnِjgْlٱ", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "فَزَادُوهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhwُdāَzَf", "root": "زيد"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "رَهَقًا", "translit": "āًqَhَr", "root": "رهق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "وَأَنَّهُمْ ظَنُّوا۟ كَمَا ظَنَنتُمْ أَن لَّن يَبْعَثَ ٱللَّهُ أَحَدًا ", "translation": "And they had thought, as you thought, that Allāh would never send anyone [as a messenger].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ظَنُّوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُّnَẓ", "root": "ظنن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَمَا", "translit": "āَmَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ظَنَنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnَnَẓ", "root": "ظنن"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَّن", "translit": "nَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَبْعَثَ", "translit": "َhtَʿعْbَy", "root": "بعث"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَحَدًا", "translit": "āًdَḥَaʾ", "root": "احد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "وَأَنَّا لَمَسْنَا ٱلسَّمَآءَ فَوَجَدْنَٰهَا مُلِئَتْ حَرَسًا شَدِيدًا وَشُهُبًا ", "translation": "And we have sought [to reach] the heaven but found it filled with powerful guards and burning flames.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَمَسْنَا", "translit": "āَnْsَmَl", "root": "لمس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَوَجَدْنَٰهَا", "translit": "āَhَٰnْdَjgَwَf", "root": "وجد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مُلِئَتْ", "translit": "ْtَyʾِlُm", "root": "ملا"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "حَرَسًا", "translit": "āًsَrَḥ", "root": "حرس"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "شَدِيدًا", "translit": "āًdyِdَhs", "root": "شدد"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَشُهُبًا", "translit": "āًbُhُhsَw", "root": "شهب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "وَأَنَّا كُنَّا نَقْعُدُ مِنْهَا مَقَٰعِدَ لِلسَّمْعِۖ فَمَن يَسْتَمِعِ ٱلْءَانَ يَجِدْ لَهُۥ شِهَابًا رَّصَدًا ", "translation": "And we used to sit therein in positions for hearing,[1] but whoever listens now will find a burning flame lying in wait for him.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَقْعُدُ", "translit": "ُdُʿعْqَn", "root": "قعد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنْهَا", "translit": "āَhْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَقَٰعِدَ", "translit": "َdِʿعَٰqَm", "root": "قعد"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لِلسَّمْعِ", "translit": "ِʿعْmَّslِl", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فَمَن", "translit": "nَmَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَسْتَمِعِ", "translit": "ِʿعِmَtْsَy", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْءَانَ", "translit": "َnāَءْlٱ", "root": "اون"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يَجِدْ", "translit": "ْdِjgَy", "root": "وجد"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "شِهَابًا", "translit": "āًbāَhِhs", "root": "شهب"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "رَّصَدًا", "translit": "āًdَṣَّr", "root": "رصد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "وَأَنَّا لَا نَدْرِىٓ أَشَرٌّ أُرِيدَ بِمَن فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ أَمْ أَرَادَ بِهِمْ رَبُّهُمْ رَشَدًا ", "translation": "And we do not know [therefore] whether evil is intended for those on earth or whether their Lord intends for them a right course.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَدْرِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِrْdَn", "root": "دري"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَشَرٌّ", "translit": "ٌّrَhsَaʾ", "root": "شرر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أُرِيدَ", "translit": "َdyِrُaʾ", "root": "رود"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِمَن", "translit": "nَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَرَادَ", "translit": "َdāَrَaʾ", "root": "رود"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "رَبُّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "رَشَدًا", "translit": "āًdَhsَr", "root": "رشد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "وَأَنَّا مِنَّا ٱلصَّٰلِحُونَ وَمِنَّا دُونَ ذَٰلِكَۖ كُنَّا طَرَآئِقَ قِدَدًا ", "translation": "And among us are the righteous, and among us are [others] not so; we were [of] divided ways.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰلِحُونَ", "translit": "َnwُḥِlَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَمِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "دُونَ", "translit": "َnwُd", "root": "دون"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "كُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "طَرَآئِقَ", "translit": "َqِyʾٓāَrَṭ", "root": "طرق"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "قِدَدًا", "translit": "āًdَdِq", "root": "قدد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 12, "text": "وَأَنَّا ظَنَنَّآ أَن لَّن نُّعْجِزَ ٱللَّهَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَلَن نُّعْجِزَهُۥ هَرَبًا ", "translation": "And we have become certain that we will never cause failure to Allāh upon earth, nor can we escape Him by flight.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ظَنَنَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّnَnَẓ", "root": "ظنن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَّن", "translit": "nَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "نُّعْجِزَ", "translit": "َzِjgْʿعُّn", "root": "عجز"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَلَن", "translit": "nَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "نُّعْجِزَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَzِjgْʿعُّn", "root": "عجز"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "هَرَبًا", "translit": "āًbَrَh", "root": "هرب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 13, "text": "وَأَنَّا لَمَّا سَمِعْنَا ٱلْهُدَىٰٓ ءَامَنَّا بِهِۦۖ فَمَن يُؤْمِنۢ بِرَبِّهِۦ فَلَا يَخَافُ بَخْسًا وَلَا رَهَقًا ", "translation": "And when we heard the guidance [i.e., the Qur’ān], we believed in it. And whoever believes in his Lord will not fear deprivation or burden.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "سَمِعْنَا", "translit": "āَnْʿعِmَs", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْهُدَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَdُhْlٱ", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ءَامَنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فَمَن", "translit": "nَmَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يُؤْمِنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِmْwʾُy", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "بِرَبِّهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِّbَrِb", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يَخَافُ", "translit": "ُfāَhkَy", "root": "خوف"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "بَخْسًا", "translit": "āًsْhkَb", "root": "بخس"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "رَهَقًا", "translit": "āًqَhَr", "root": "رهق"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 14, "text": "وَأَنَّا مِنَّا ٱلْمُسْلِمُونَ وَمِنَّا ٱلْقَٰسِطُونَۖ فَمَنْ أَسْلَمَ فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ تَحَرَّوْا۟ رَشَدًا ", "translation": "And among us are Muslims [in submission to Allāh], and among us are the unjust.[1] And whoever has become Muslim - those have sought out the right course.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمُسْلِمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmِlْsُmْlٱ", "root": "سلم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَمِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْقَٰسِطُونَ", "translit": "َnwُṭِsَٰqْlٱ", "root": "قسط"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَمَنْ", "translit": "ْnَmَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَسْلَمَ", "translit": "َmَlْsَaʾ", "root": "سلم"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "تَحَرَّوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَّrَḥَt", "root": "حري"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رَشَدًا", "translit": "āًdَhsَr", "root": "رشد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 15, "text": "وَأَمَّا ٱلْقَٰسِطُونَ فَكَانُوا۟ لِجَهَنَّمَ حَطَبًا ", "translation": "But as for the unjust, they will be, for Hell, firewood.'", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْقَٰسِطُونَ", "translit": "َnwُṭِsَٰqْlٱ", "root": "قسط"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَكَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَkَf", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لِجَهَنَّمَ", "translit": "َmَّnَhَjgِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "حَطَبًا", "translit": "āًbَṭَḥ", "root": "حطب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 16, "text": "وَأَلَّوِ ٱسْتَقَٰمُوا۟ عَلَى ٱلطَّرِيقَةِ لَأَسْقَيْنَٰهُم مَّآءً غَدَقًا ", "translation": "And [Allāh revealed] that if they had remained straight on the way, We would have given them abundant rain [i.e., provision]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَلَّوِ", "translit": "ِwَّlَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱسْتَقَٰمُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُmَٰqَtْsٱ", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَى", "translit": "àَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلطَّرِيقَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَqyِrَّṭlٱ", "root": "طرق"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَأَسْقَيْنَٰهُم", "translit": "mُhَٰnْyَqْsَaʾَl", "root": "سقي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مَّآءً", "translit": "ًءٓāَّm", "root": "موه"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "غَدَقًا", "translit": "āًqَdَغ", "root": "غدق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 17, "text": "لِّنَفْتِنَهُمْ فِيهِۚ وَمَن يُعْرِضْ عَن ذِكْرِ رَبِّهِۦ يَسْلُكْهُ عَذَابًا صَعَدًا ", "translation": "So We might test them therein. And whoever turns away from the remembrance of his Lord[1] He will put into arduous punishment.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لِّنَفْتِنَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَnِtْfَnِّl", "root": "فتن"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يُعْرِضْ", "translit": "ْḍِrْʿعُy", "root": "عرض"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ذِكْرِ", "translit": "ِrْkِhd", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "رَبِّهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَسْلُكْهُ", "translit": "ُhْkُlْsَy", "root": "سلك"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عَذَابًا", "translit": "āًbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "صَعَدًا", "translit": "āًdَʿعَṣ", "root": "صعد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 18, "text": "وَأَنَّ ٱلْمَسَٰجِدَ لِلَّهِ فَلَا تَدْعُوا۟ مَعَ ٱللَّهِ أَحَدًا ", "translation": "And [He revealed] that the masjids[1] are for Allāh, so do not invoke[2] with Allāh anyone.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْمَسَٰجِدَ", "translit": "َdِjgَٰsَmْlٱ", "root": "سجد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِl", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَدْعُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُʿعْdَt", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مَعَ", "translit": "َʿعَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَحَدًا", "translit": "āًdَḥَaʾ", "root": "احد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 19, "text": "وَأَنَّهُۥ لَمَّا قَامَ عَبْدُ ٱللَّهِ يَدْعُوهُ كَادُوا۟ يَكُونُونَ عَلَيْهِ لِبَدًا ", "translation": "And that when the Servant [i.e., Prophet] of Allāh stood up supplicating Him, they almost became about him a compacted mass.\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قَامَ", "translit": "َmāَq", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَبْدُ", "translit": "ُdْbَʿع", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَدْعُوهُ", "translit": "ُhwُʿعْdَy", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "كَادُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُdāَk", "root": "كود"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَكُونُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnwُkَy", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لِبَدًا", "translit": "āًdَbِl", "root": "لبد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 20, "text": "قُلْ إِنَّمَآ أَدْعُوا۟ رَبِّى وَلَآ أُشْرِكُ بِهِۦٓ أَحَدًا ", "translation": "Say, [O Muḥammad], \"I only invoke my Lord and do not associate with Him anyone.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَدْعُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُʿعْdَaʾ", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "رَبِّى", "translit": "àِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أُشْرِكُ", "translit": "ُkِrْhsُaʾ", "root": "شرك"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَحَدًا", "translit": "āًdَḥَaʾ", "root": "احد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 21, "text": "قُلْ إِنِّى لَآ أَمْلِكُ لَكُمْ ضَرًّا وَلَا رَشَدًا ", "translation": "Say, \"Indeed, I do not possess for you [the power of] harm or right direction.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَآ", "translit": "ٓāَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَمْلِكُ", "translit": "ُkِlْmَaʾ", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ضَرًّا", "translit": "āًّrَḍ", "root": "ضرر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "رَشَدًا", "translit": "āًdَhsَr", "root": "رشد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 22, "text": "قُلْ إِنِّى لَن يُجِيرَنِى مِنَ ٱللَّهِ أَحَدٌ وَلَنْ أَجِدَ مِن دُونِهِۦ مُلْتَحَدًا ", "translation": "Say, \"Indeed, there will never protect me from Allāh anyone [if I should disobey], nor will I find in other than Him a refuge.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَن", "translit": "nَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يُجِيرَنِى", "translit": "àِnَryِjgُy", "root": "جور"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَحَدٌ", "translit": "ٌdَḥَaʾ", "root": "احد"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَلَنْ", "translit": "ْnَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَجِدَ", "translit": "َdِjgَaʾ", "root": "وجد"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "دُونِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِnwُd", "root": "دون"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مُلْتَحَدًا", "translit": "āًdَḥَtْlُm", "root": "لحد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 23, "text": "إِلَّا بَلَٰغًا مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَرِسَٰلَٰتِهِۦۚ وَمَن يَعْصِ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ فَإِنَّ لَهُۥ نَارَ جَهَنَّمَ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَآ أَبَدًا ", "translation": "But [I have for you] only notification from Allāh, and His messages.\" And whoever disobeys Allāh and His Messenger - then indeed, for him is the fire of Hell; they will abide therein forever.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَلَٰغًا", "translit": "āًغَٰlَb", "root": "بلغ"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَرِسَٰلَٰتِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِtَٰlَٰsِrَw", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَعْصِ", "translit": "ِṣْʿعَy", "root": "عصي"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَرَسُولَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَlwُsَrَw", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "فَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "نَارَ", "translit": "َrāَn", "root": "نور"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "جَهَنَّمَ", "translit": "َmَّnَhَjg", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "خَٰلِدِينَ", "translit": "َnyِdِlَٰhk", "root": "خلد"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "فِيهَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "أَبَدًا", "translit": "āًdَbَaʾ", "root": "ابد"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 24, "text": "حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا رَأَوْا۟ مَا يُوعَدُونَ فَسَيَعْلَمُونَ مَنْ أَضْعَفُ نَاصِرًا وَأَقَلُّ عَدَدًا ", "translation": "[The disbelievers continue] until, when they see that which they are promised, then they will know who is weaker in helpers and less in number.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَأَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَaʾَr", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يُوعَدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdَʿعwُy", "root": "وعد"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَسَيَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْʿعَyَsَf", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مَنْ", "translit": "ْnَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَضْعَفُ", "translit": "ُfَʿعْḍَaʾ", "root": "ضعف"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "نَاصِرًا", "translit": "āًrِṣāَn", "root": "نصر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَأَقَلُّ", "translit": "ُّlَqَaʾَw", "root": "قلل"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "عَدَدًا", "translit": "āًdَdَʿع", "root": "عدد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 25, "text": "قُلْ إِنْ أَدْرِىٓ أَقَرِيبٌ مَّا تُوعَدُونَ أَمْ يَجْعَلُ لَهُۥ رَبِّىٓ أَمَدًا ", "translation": "Say, \"I do not know if what you are promised is near or if my Lord will grant for it a [long] period.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَدْرِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِrْdَaʾ", "root": "دري"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَقَرِيبٌ", "translit": "ٌbyِrَqَaʾ", "root": "قرب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تُوعَدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdَʿعwُt", "root": "وعد"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَجْعَلُ", "translit": "ُlَʿعْjgَy", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رَبِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَمَدًا", "translit": "āًdَmَaʾ", "root": "امد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 26, "text": "عَٰلِمُ ٱلْغَيْبِ فَلَا يُظْهِرُ عَلَىٰ غَيْبِهِۦٓ أَحَدًا ", "translation": "[He is] Knower of the unseen, and He does not disclose His [knowledge of the] unseen to anyone", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "عَٰلِمُ", "translit": "ُmِlَٰʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْغَيْبِ", "translit": "ِbْyَغْlٱ", "root": "غيب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يُظْهِرُ", "translit": "ُrِhْẓُy", "root": "ظهر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "غَيْبِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِbْyَغ", "root": "غيب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَحَدًا", "translit": "āًdَḥَaʾ", "root": "احد"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 27, "text": "إِلَّا مَنِ ٱرْتَضَىٰ مِن رَّسُولٍ فَإِنَّهُۥ يَسْلُكُ مِنۢ بَيْنِ يَدَيْهِ وَمِنْ خَلْفِهِۦ رَصَدًا ", "translation": "Except whom He has approved of messengers, and indeed, He sends before him [i.e., each messenger] and behind him observers[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَنِ", "translit": "ِnَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱرْتَضَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَḍَtْrٱ", "root": "رضو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رَّسُولٍ", "translit": "ٍlwُsَّr", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَإِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَسْلُكُ", "translit": "ُkُlْsَy", "root": "سلك"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "بَيْنِ", "translit": "ِnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يَدَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَdَy", "root": "يدي"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَمِنْ", "translit": "ْnِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "خَلْفِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِfْlَhk", "root": "خلف"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "رَصَدًا", "translit": "āًdَṣَr", "root": "رصد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 28, "text": "لِّيَعْلَمَ أَن قَدْ أَبْلَغُوا۟ رِسَٰلَٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ وَأَحَاطَ بِمَا لَدَيْهِمْ وَأَحْصَىٰ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ عَدَدًۢا ", "translation": "That he [i.e., Muḥammad (ﷺ)] may know[1] that they have conveyed the messages of their Lord; and He has encompassed whatever is with them and has enumerated all things in number.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لِّيَعْلَمَ", "translit": "َmَlْʿعَyِّl", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قَدْ", "translit": "ْdَq", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَبْلَغُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُغَlْbَaʾ", "root": "بلغ"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رِسَٰلَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰlَٰsِr", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "رَبِّهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَأَحَاطَ", "translit": "َṭāَḥَaʾَw", "root": "حوط"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَدَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَdَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَأَحْصَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَṣْḥَaʾَw", "root": "حصي"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "كُلَّ", "translit": "َّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "شَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "عَدَدًۢا", "translit": "āًۢdَdَʿع", "root": "عدد"}], "hasIhya": true}], "tafsir": {"1": [{"arabic": "هو الذي أرشد الأولين والآخرين ولما سمعه الجن لم يلبثوا أن ولوا إلى قومهم منذرين فقالوا إنا سمعنا قرآنا عجبا يهدي إلى الرشد فآمنا به ولن نشرك بربنا أحدا فكل من آمن به فقد وفق ومن قال به فقد صدق ومن تمسك به فقد هدي ومن عمل به فقد فاز", "english": "It is the one that guided the first and the last, and when the Jinn heard it, they did not delay in turning back to their people as warners, and they said: 'Indeed, we have heard a wondrous Quran that guides to the right path (Rushd), so we have believed in it, and we will not associate with our Lord anyone.' So everyone who believes in it has been granted success (Waffaqa), and everyone who speaks by it has spoken truthfully, and everyone who holds fast to it has been guided, and everyone who acts by it has attained success.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-8.doc.txt", "book_title": "Etiquette of Quran Recitation", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications and their spiritual significance, from 'Etiquette of Quran Recitation'", "badge": "Du'a"}], "13": [{"arabic": "فإن قلت: فما شبهة المعتزلة والمرجئة وما حجة بطلان قولهم. فأقول شبهتهم عمومات القرآن أما المرجئة فقالوا لا يدخل المؤمن النار وإن أتي بكل المعاصي لقوله عز وجل: ﴿ فمن يؤمن بربه فلا يخاف بخسا ولا رهقا ﴾ {} ولقوله سبحانه وتعالى: ﴿ والذين آمنوا بالله ورسله أولئك هم الصديقون ﴾ {} الآية ولقوله تعالى: ﴿ كلما ألقي فيها فوج سألهم خزنتها. ﴾ {} إلى قوله: ﴿ فكذبنا وقلنا ما نزل الله من شيء ﴾ {} فقوله كلما ألقي فيها فوج عام فينبغي أن يكون من ألقي في النار مكذبا ولقوله تعالى: ﴿ لا يصلاها إلا الأشقى الذي كذب وتول", "english": "If you say: What is the doubt of the Mu'tazila and the Murji'a and what is the proof of the invalidity of their statement? I say: Their doubt is generalities of the Quran. As for the Murji'a, they said: The believer does not enter the Fire even if he commits all sins, due to His saying, the Mighty and Majestic: 'So whoever believes in his Lord, he does not fear loss (bakhsan) nor oppression (rahqan).' And due to His saying, the Blessed and Exalted: 'And those who believe in Allah and His messengers - those are the truthful ones.' The verse. And due to His saying: 'Every time a group is thrown into it, its keepers will ask them...' until His saying: 'So we denied and said: Allah has not sent down anything.' So His saying 'Every time a group is thrown into it' is general, so it should be that whoever is thrown into the Fire is a denier. And due to His saying: 'None will burn in it except the most wretched, who denied and turned away.' And this is restriction, affirmation, and negation. And due to His saying: 'Whoever comes with a good deed will have better than it, and they will be safe from fear that Day.' So faith (Iman) is the head of good deeds. And due to His saying: 'And Allah loves the doers of good (Muhsinin).' And He said: 'Indeed, We do not waste the reward of one who does good work.' And they have no proof in that, for wherever faith (Iman) is mentioned in these verses, it is intended to be faith (Iman) with action, since we have clarified that faith (Iman) may be used and intended to mean Islam, which is agreement with the heart (Qalb), speech, and action. The evidence for this interpretation is many reports about punishing the disobedient and the measures of punishment, and his saying (peace be upon him): 'He will be taken out of the Fire whoever has in his heart (Qalb) an atom's weight of faith (Iman).' So how can he be taken out if he did not enter? And from the Quran, His saying: 'Indeed, Allah does not forgive association with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills.' And the exception with will indicates division.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Foundations of Belief", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Foundations of Belief'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "23": [{"arabic": "وأما المعتزلة فشبهتهم قوله تعالى: ﴿ وإني لغفار لمن تاب وآمن وعمل صالحا ثم اهتدى ﴾ {} وقوله تعالى: ﴿ والعصر إن الإنسان لفي خسر إلا الذين آمنوا وعملوا الصالحات ﴾ {} وقوله تعالى ﴿ وإن منكم إلا واردها كان على ربك حتما مقضيا ﴾ {} ثم قال: ﴿ ثم ننجي الذين اتقوا ﴾ {} وقوله تعالى: ﴿ ومن يعص الله ورسوله فإن له نار جهنم ﴾ {} وكل آية ذكر الله عز وجل العمل الصالح فيها مقرونا بالإيمان وقوله تعالى: ﴿ ومن يقتل مؤمنا متعمدا فجزاؤه جهنم خالدا فيها ﴾ {} وهذه العمومات أيضا مخصوصة بدليل قوله تعالى: ﴿ ويغفر ما دون ذل", "english": "As for the Mu'tazilites, their evidence is His saying, the Exalted: 'Indeed, I am Forgiving to whoever repents and believes and does righteous deeds then remains guided' and His saying, the Exalted: 'By time, indeed, mankind is in loss, except for those who have believed and done righteous deeds' and His saying, the Exalted: 'And there is none of you except he will enter it; it has been upon your Lord a decree determined' then He said: 'Then We will save those who feared' and His saying, the Exalted: 'And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger, then indeed, for him is the Fire of Hell' and every verse in which Allah, the Exalted, mentions righteous deeds coupled with faith and His saying, the Exalted: 'And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell, abiding therein eternally' and these generalities are also specified by the evidence of His saying, the Exalted: 'And He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills' so it is appropriate that His will remains in forgiving what is besides polytheism and likewise His saying: 'He will bring out of the Fire whoever had in his heart an atom's weight of faith' and His saying, the Exalted: 'Indeed, We do not waste the reward of one who does good deeds' and His saying, the Exalted: 'Indeed, Allah does not waste the reward of the doers of good' so how would He waste the reward of the foundation of faith and all acts of obedience with a single disobedience and His saying, the Exalted: 'And whoever kills a believer intentionally' meaning because of his faith and it has come regarding such a cause.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Foundations of Belief", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Foundations of Belief'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "وخطب رجل عند رسول الله ﭬ فقال: من يطع الله ورسوله فقد رشد ومن يعصهما فقد غوى\"[257] فقال \"قل: ومن يعص الله ورسوله فقد غوى فكره رسول الله ﭬ قوله: ومن يعصهما، لأنه تسوية وجمع.", "english": "And a man delivered a sermon in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: 'Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has been guided, and whoever disobeys them has gone astray.' He (peace be upon him) said: 'Say: And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger has gone astray.' The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) disliked his saying: 'and whoever disobeys them,' because it is an equalization and a joining together.", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book4a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Condemnation of Anger and Hatred", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Condemnation of Anger and Hatred'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "وقوله تعالى: ﴿ ومن يعص الله ورسوله فإن له نار جهنم خالدين فيها ﴾ {} وتخصيصه بالكفر تحكم", "english": "And His saying, the Exalted: 'And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger, then for him is the Fire of Hell, abiding therein eternally' {} and specifying it as disbelief is arbitrary judgment.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Foundations of Belief", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Foundations of Belief'", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "26": [{"arabic": "وما غاب عن الأبصار فيعبر عنه بالغيب والملكوت والله تعالى عالم الغيب والشهادة وجبار الملك والملكوت ولا يحيط أحد بشىء من علمه إلا بما شاء وهو عالم الغيب فلا يظهر على غيبه أحدا إلا من ارتضى من رسول فأجل أيها العاقل فكر فى الملكوت فعسى يفتح لك ابواب السماء فتجول بقلبك فى أقطارها إلى أن يقوم قلبك بين يدي عرش الرحمن", "english": "And what is hidden from the sights is expressed as the Unseen (Al-Ghayb) and the Dominion (Al-Malakut), and Allah the Exalted is the Knower of the Unseen (Al-Ghayb) and the Witnessed (Al-Shahadah), and the Compeller of the Kingdom (Al-Mulk) and the Dominion (Al-Malakut). And no one encompasses anything of His knowledge except by what He wills, and He is the Knower of the Unseen (Al-Ghayb), so He does not reveal His Unseen (Ghayb) to anyone except to a messenger whom He has approved. Therefore, O intelligent one, contemplate in the Dominion (Al-Malakut), so perhaps the doors of the heaven will be opened for you, and you will wander with your Heart (Qalb) in its regions until your Heart (Qalb) stands before the Throne of the Most Merciful.", "book_file": "vol4_j4-k09.doc.txt", "book_title": "Contemplation", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Contemplation'", "badge": "Insight"}], "28": [{"arabic": "اللهم إني أعوذ بك من شر نفسي ومن شر كل دابة أنت آخذ بناصيتها إن ربي على صراط مستقيم", "english": "O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul (Nafs) and from the evil of every creature whose forelock You hold. Indeed, my Lord is upon a straight path.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-9.doc.txt", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith", "badge": "Insight"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 400, 971], [2, 971, 2347], [3, 2347, 3599], [4, 3599, 4780], [5, 4780, 5974], [6, 5974, 6753], [7, 6753, 7649], [8, 7649, 8882], [9, 8882, 11556], [10, 11556, 12919], [11, 12919, 14451], [12, 14451, 16320], [13, 16320, 17565]], "2": [[1, 400, 2293], [2, 2293, 3253], [3, 3253, 4615], [4, 4615, 6677], [5, 6677, 7170], [6, 7170, 8078], [7, 8078, 9543], [8, 9543, 11854], [9, 11854, 13124]], "3": [[1, 400, 2030], [2, 2030, 3733], [3, 3733, 4474], [4, 4474, 5916], [5, 5916, 6617], [6, 6617, 7762], [7, 7762, 9104], [8, 9104, 10209], [9, 10209, 11583]], "4": [[1, 400, 1805], [2, 1805, 2641], [3, 2641, 3848], [4, 3848, 5497], [5, 5497, 6356], [6, 6356, 7